\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Iceland \highlight\uc2 's c.bank keeps rate steady, says may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market\b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2018\par 11:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 COPENHAGEN, Dec 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Iceland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday kept its deposit rate unchanged at 4.50 percent and said it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the planned release of offshore crown assets weakens the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Plans were announced last week to release the last of offshore crown assets that were locked in by capital controls in the aftermath of the financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 The Finance Ministry proposed to expand authorisations for withdrawals from accounts that are subject to restrictions that were put in place when the capital controls began to be lifted in 2016.\par \par \uc2 "The resolution of such a legacy problem should not be allowed to lower the exchange rate of the crown; therefore, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "In this context, the Bank will also take into consideration that there are signs that the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation has pushed the real exchange rate below its equilibrium value."\par \par \uc2 The crown has weakened over the last seven months so that a U.S. dollar now costs 123 crowns from below 100 crowns in April.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the rate a month ago from 4.25 percent, its first rate move in more than a year.\par \par \uc2 "If inflation expectations continue to rise and remain persistently at a level above the target, it will call for a tighter monetary stance," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday. (Reporting by Teis Jensen Editing by Jacob Gronholt-Pedersen and Peter Graff) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-12-12T11:02:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020181212eecc01ky1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
