\par\par \b \uc2 *\uc2 Iceland  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Keeps Key Rate at 4.5%\b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2018\par 09:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2018 03:56 ET *\uc2 Iceland \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : GDP Growth Measured 5% For First Nine Months of Yr, Slightly Higher Than Assumed in Nov Forecast\par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2018 03:58 ET *\uc2 Iceland \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : ISK Depreciation, Concerns Over Upcoming Wage Settlements Have Shown in Expectations of Further Rise in Inflation\par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2018 03:58 ET *\uc2 Iceland \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Monetary Stance as Measured by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Real Rate Has Therefore Eased Again\par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2018 03:59 ET *\uc2 Iceland \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Signs That Positive Output Gap Will Continue to Narrow in Near Term\par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2018 03:59 ET *\uc2 Iceland \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Rise in Inflation Expectations Limited to Short-Term Expectations, Depreciation of ISK Has Slowed\par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2018 04:02 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 Iceland Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Says Will \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market, In Line With Previous Statements\par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2018 04:03 ET *\uc2 Iceland \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Will Also Consider There Are Signs Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Depreciation Has Pushed Real Exchange Rate Below Equilibrium Value\par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2018 04:03 ET *\uc2 Iceland \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Near-Term Monetary Stance Depends on Narrower Output Gap, Wage-Setting Decisions, Devts in Inflation and Inflation Expectations\par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2018 04:04 ET *\uc2 Iceland \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Says Has The Will and The Tools to Keep Inflation at Target Over Long Term\par \par \uc2 12 Dec 2018 04:42 ET  \uc2 Iceland's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Leaves Key Rate Unchanged at 4.50%\par \par \uc2 By Nina Adam\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Icelandic \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left the key rate unchanged at 4.50% on Wednesday, but signaled that it is prepared to act if inflation expectation continue to nudge higher.\par \par \uc2 "The near-term monetary stance will depend on the interaction between a narrower output gap, wage-setting decisions, and developments in inflation and inflation expectations," said the Sedlabanki, after raising the key rate by 0.25 percentage points in early November.\par \par \uc2 The Monetary Policy Committee has "the will and the necessary tools to keep inflation at target over the long term," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Inflation in the north Atlantic island is running well above the Sedlabanki's 2.5% target, measuring 3.3% in November, underpinned by solid economic growth and a steep rise in import prices.\par \par \uc2 In addition, a significant depreciation of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the course of this year and expectations of strong wage settlements in upcoming negations have pushed up inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 "If inflation expectations continue to rise and remain persistently at a level above the target, it will call for a tighter monetary stance," said the Sedlabanki.\par \par \uc2 Dominic Chopping contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Nina Adam at nina.adam@wsj.com<mailto:nina.adam@wsj.com>\par \par \uc2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 12, 2018 04:42 ET (09:42 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument D