\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-INTERVIEW-Iceland wants to avoid more  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  falls-cbank head\b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2013\par 09:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story filed late on Monday, with no changes)\par \par \uc2 * Iceland cbank head "to lean" against depreciation\par \par \uc2 * Interest rate rise unlikely in coming months\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness is key concern of bank\par \par \uc2 By Alistair Scrutton\par \par \uc2 REYKJAVIK, Feb 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Iceland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure as little depreciation as possible in its weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to inflation concerns but will draw no line in the sand over the crown's value, its governor Mar Gudmundsson said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Gudmundsson told Reuters the introduction of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , announced last week by the bank, would likely mean there would be no rise in interest rates in the coming months, helping prop up weaker-than-expected economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last week it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the crown and control inflation after shaving back growth forecasts for an economy recovering from a 2008 bank crisis. The crown was at its lowest in trade-weighted terms since an economic recovery began.\par \par \uc2 "We will resist it, we will lean against depreciation", Gudmundsson said. "Preferably we want to have as little depreciation as possible."\par \par \uc2 Hit by a banking crisis in 2008-9, Iceland has bounced back better than many European economies after a huge fall in the crown, the imposition of capital controls and avoiding expensive bank rescues. But the bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was now the main source of uncertainty in the economy.\par \par \uc2 "The exchange rate is very much key," the governor added. "It is below what you need for a kind of sustainable equilibrium in the economy."\par \par \uc2 The bank has said recent weakness was due to a lower trade surplus and a build up of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for foreign loan payments in a county where many loans are not in crowns.\par \par \uc2 "The depreciation we would be willing to accept is limited but that will depend on conditions. If the terms of trade continue to weaken then we will have to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken with it," Gudmundsson said.\par \par \uc2 "But the prediction is that (terms of trade) will stabilise and actually improve somewhat in the second quarter. If that doesn't happen we will have to revise how we look at the exchange rate."\par \par \uc2 Given these prospects, Gudmundsson said, the bank was trying to avoid the exchange rate depreciating too much.\par \par \uc2 "It is a smoothing exercise that has more of an imperative because of the fact we have inflation well above target and growth prospects have weakened somewhat," he added.\par \par \uc2 The bank expects inflation to average 3.8 percent this year, slightly more than expected in a November forecast, and ranging between 3 percent and 4 percent through mid-2014 in line with the last forecast.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasts 2012 gross domestic product growth of 2.2 percent rather than 2.5 percent expected in November and for 2.1 percent this year rather than 3 percent.\par \par \uc2 Given slowing growth, the governor said it was unlikely interest rates would rise.\par \par \uc2 "It is very unlikely that we will increase rates in coming months, even to the end of this year ... but you don't know what can hit us and monetary policy is always reassessed," the governor said.\par \par \uc2 "We would try to avoid if possible having to tighten monetary policy on top of a weakening economy and that is why we are temporarily using \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an extra tool," he added.\par \par \uc2 Economists say there is no imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis and the bank is trying to counteract seasonal weakness, with tourism revenues traditionally low in the winter.\par \par \uc2 Previously the bank held regular scheduled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, which were meant to be exchange rate neutral. It has also been holding auctions of crowns and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help reduce foreign investor holdings of Icelandic crowns, left after capital controls were introduced following the crisis.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Andrew Heavens)\par \par \uc2 ICELAND-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (INTERVIEW) (REPEAT) | DA | FN | NW | SW | ABN | D | M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130215e92c000fw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
