\par\par \b \uc2 Iceland c. bank head demands leaning to avoid bubbles\b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2010\par 20:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT, Dec 2 (Reuters) - Central banks should work actively to fend off asset bubbles to avoid boom and bust cycles, even if overall inflation is within targets, Iceland \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Mar Gudmundsson said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 He also said he was not sure whether bailing out holders of commercial banks' bonds in insolvency would be the right decision for every country, but was necessary for Iceland.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation targeting is not enough," Gudmundsson said at an event organised by the Goethe University Frankfurt.\par \par \uc2 "We should lean as well as clean ... We need inflation targeting plus," he said, and added the "plus" represents additional tools, such as limiting capital inflows, active \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and having large budget surpluses.\par \par \uc2 Reflecting on \b \highlight22\uc2 Iceland\b0 \highlight\uc2  banking collapse in October 2008, he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should have restricted capital from coming into the country.\par \par \uc2 "We should have leaned against the capital inflows that were taking place," he said. Iceland's three commercial banks failed in October 2008 and were placed in special resolution regimes, throwing the tiny country into its worst recession since World War II.\par \par \uc2 The government did not bail out bondholders.\par \par \uc2 "I haven't made up my mind whether it is the right decision for everybody," he said. "But Iceland didn't have any other option," referring to the size of banks dwarfing the size of the country's economy, which made a bailout impossible.\par \par \uc2 Gudmundsson also said governments should not be afraid to carry large budget surpluses when times are good to prepare for the downturn.\par \par \uc2 "We should not be afraid of big government surpluses during booms," he said. (Reporting by Sakari Suoninen; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 ICELAND/CENTRALBANK|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101202e6c2001eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
