\par\par \b \uc2 Iceland cbank sees scope for further easing of policy\b0\par\par\uc2 168 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2009\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  STOCKHOLM, Dec 10 (Reuters) - Iceland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday there would be scope for gradual monetary easing if the crown remains stable or appreciates as it has done since its last meeting in November.\par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it remained ready to adjust its stance as required to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keep inflation under control.\par \par \uc2  Sedlabanki said in a statement it had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since early November.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Iceland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier on Thursday it cut its key interest rates by one percentage point to 10 percent.\par \par \uc2  In addition to the one-point reduction in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's seven-day collateral lending rate, the Sedlabanki also lowered its overnight lending rate by 1.5 percentage points to 11.5 percent and cut its deposit rate by half a point to 8.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 ICELAND-POLICY/ (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW|E|RBN|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091210e5ca000pa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
