\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Markets-Stocks at 4-week high,  \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  bond due   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn   \par \uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2008\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, April 2 (Reuters) - Emerging equities jumped nearly 2 percent to four-week highs on Wednesday as investors took a more upbeat view on risk, while an expected bond for  \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  signalled a reopening of the emerging sovereign bond market.   \par \par \uc2 Markets calmed after  \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  raised $4 billion of capital on Tuesday, quelling some speculation that it might be in trouble [nL02733264].   \par \par \uc2 The rand hit three-week highs, buoyed also by data showing a slowing in domestic credit growth demand, and the Turkish lira rallied nearly 1 percent from the U.S. close.   \par \par \uc2 "All the equity and credit markets are very closely correlated at the moment and there was a strong rally yesterday," said Kasper Bartholdy, head of sovereign strategy at  \uc2 Credit Suisse.\par \par \uc2 "We are still going to see the markets trading on-and-off over the next couple of months."   \par \par \uc2 Benchmark emerging equities <.MSCIEF> hit their best level since early March, while emerging sovereign debt spreads tightened by 4 basis points to 292 bps over U.S. Treasuries <11EMJ>, after narrowing 12 bps into Tuesday's U.S. close.   \par \par \uc2 Russia's  \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  may price a benchmark two-tranche dollar bond totalling up to $1.5 billion later on Wednesday, a banking source said, and analysts said steadying debt spreads may encourage more borrowers to the market.   \par \par \uc2 Initial yield guidance is for the five-year tranche to be priced at 400 basis points over mid-swaps and the 10-year tranche at 400-425 bps over mid-swaps, banking sources said.   \par \par \uc2 The bond will be lead managed by Citi and  \uc2 Morgan Stanley.\par \par \uc2 Investors are also on the look-out for a $500 million debut Eurobond from Georgia, lead managed by  \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  and  \uc2 UBS.\par \par \uc2 ICELAND UNFREEZING?   \par \par \uc2 The Icelandic crown rose more than 2 percent against the euro <EURISK=> and the dollar <ISK=> after Iceland's prime minister Geir Haarde told the Financial Times \b \highlight22\uc2 Iceland\b0 \highlight\uc2  may consider direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in money and equity markets to protect the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial system.   \par \par \uc2 "The government will have to provide in one form or another and then they can break the vicious circle the markets have been in," said Beat Siegenthaler, senior strategist at TD Securities.   \par \par \uc2 The Icelandic crown has fallen 25 percent this year as investors and ratings agencies fret over the state of Iceland's banking system.   \par \par \uc2 The Czech crown rose slightly against the euro <EURCZK=> but hung below four-week highs set this week.   \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry is fine-tuning an agreement with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on capping the crown, which has risen sharply on strong exports and economic growth. The text may be published in days, finance minister Miroslav Kalousek said late on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty rose to a six-year high against the euro <EURPLN=>, buoyed by strengthening risk appetite and by the Polish lower house of parliament's backing on Tuesday of the European Union's reform treaty.   \par \par \uc2 The Kenyan shilling <KES=> rose 1.5 percent and was trading close to 2008 highs, buoyed by dollar inflows from aid organisations and an ongoing share offer of a 25 percent stake in mobile phone firm Safaricom .   \par \par \uc2 Kenya's finance minister Amos Kimunya told Reuters economic growth could fall as low as 4.0-4.5 percent this year, though he still hoped for 6 percent, after ethnic clashes following a disputed presidential vote late in 2007 hurt the economy.   \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Sebastian Tong)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080405e4420008n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
