\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Iceland \highlight\uc2  crown recovers,c.bank says no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn   \par \uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 17:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 19 (Reuters) - The Icelandic crown bounced sharply in late trading in the local market on Wednesday, correcting most of the day's 6 percent losses against the euro and the dollar, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trading was volatile in the thin crown market, which has been affected by global risk aversion and worries about the local financial sector.\par \par \uc2 The latest upward moves were sharp but traders said they did not see \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It's not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 Iceland\b0 \highlight\uc2 -based trader, "it's just very volatile".\par \par \uc2 An official at the Icelandic \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not been in the market.\par \par \uc2 The crown had dropped to record lows against the euro of 127.96 <EURISK=> and five-year lows against the dollar of 81.62 <ISK=> earlier on Wednesday, but recovered to 122.05 and 78.00, down 1 percent on the day, by 1603 GMT as the local market closed.\par \par \uc2 Losses in the crown, which has fallen as much as 25 percent so far this month against the euro, had intensified on Wednesday after Icelandic financial services firm Exista offered to buy a recently listed telecoms holding company. Exista is a major shareholder in Icelandic bank Kaupthing.\par \par \uc2 "It's a bit of an unusual transaction at a bad time from one of the main investors of the biggest bank, which is already under fire," said Raffaella Tenconi, strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort.\par \par \uc2 Peter Attard Montalto, emerging markets economist at \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 , also said there were 25 billion crowns of glacier bond redemptions falling due on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "These are normally rolled or covered with new issuance and so people keep their money in the country, however there are no announced issuances or rolls. In this risk environment, people will likely withdraw their money, causing further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness," he said.\par \par \uc2 One trader said the late trading recovery may have been due to buying by local banks.\par \par \uc2 There has been speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local swaps market or possibly issue short-term Icelandic crown debt to soak up crowns in the market.\par \par \uc2 "Maybe it's (crown recovery) because people think the Icelandic crown is overshooting, or there might be some speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do something or announce something over Easter," said another Iceland-based analyst.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Adam Cox, Peter Apps, Sebastian Tong and Toni Vorobyova)\par \par \uc2 ICELAND-MARKETS (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|DA|FN|NW|SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080319e43j001bv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
