\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Iceland cenbank supports crown with dollar sales. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jon Svanur Johannsson \par \uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2001\par 20:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and economist comments, background, updates rates) \par \par \uc2  REYKJAVIK, Jan 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Iceland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, selling dollars to support the crown which has been weakening recently towards its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band limit. \par \par \uc2  The bank said in a brief statement it had sold about two billion crowns ($23.17 million) worth of dollars. \par \par \uc2  "We believed there was a good reason to demonstrate to the market that we are adamant in protecting the crown by making sure it will not exceed its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band limits," Eirikur Gudnason, one of the bank's three governors, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "Yesterday the crown weakened considerably more than usual and therefore we decided to send this message to the market." \par \par \uc2  The crown hit a record low 122.58 on Wednesday on its inverse trade-weighted index , which is closely monitored by Icelandic banks and investors, after closing below 122.2 for the first time on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the index back to 121.34, but it fell back to 122.10-15 in late trading, with the dollar at 86.25/35 crowns, off an 86.47 high and 85.32 low, after closing at 84.91 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  CLOSE TO THE LIMIT \par \par \uc2  The crown is now perilously close to its lower limit of 125.36 on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, whose central rate is 115.01. \par \par \uc2  Gudnason said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was keeping a close eye on the crown but had not yet decided on its next moves. \par \par \uc2  "I simply cannot answer what will happen next as nobody knows what is going to happen. The bank itself has made no decision whatsoever on what we will do next nor when we will do it," he said. \par \par \uc2  Islandsbanki-FBA economist Ingolfur Bender said the crown had been weakening slowly but steadily for some time for various reasons, especially the repayment of foreign loans and closure of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps. \par \par \uc2  "However, the most significant reason is that investors in general have little faith in the crown being able to maintain steadiness. Therefore, while the outflow in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is considerable, the inflow is very low," he said. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's further weakening in the crown showed the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not sufficed to stop the decline, he said. \par \par \uc2  The crown is now close to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band limits which the bank is obliged to defend, so a further weakening would provoke renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  Other options would be for the bank to change the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band limits, move the central rate, or let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float, he said. \par \par \uc2  The crown has been weakening since the end of April, but in the last few days the rate of decline has increased. \par \par \uc2  In July the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily and even suspend \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market trading after the crown fell through 112 on the index. \par \par \uc2  The bank widened the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band limits to plus or minus nine percent in February last year from plus or minus six percent to give the crown, which was strengthening at the time, more scope to appreciate to counter inflation. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx1o06w46\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
