\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Iceland \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to steady crown. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Bjarni Mar Gylfason \par \uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2000\par 16:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  REYKJAVIK, July 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Iceland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily on Friday to support the crown as the beleagured \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hit by inflation worries, sank to its lowest level since late 1996. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for the third day running, succeeded in lifting the crown from its lows, but the crown remained under pressure, prompting many in the market to forecast the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would resort to a stiff rise in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Others said the government could be forced to act, for instance by cutting public spending. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take heart from signs that some players were moving back into the market to buy crowns. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Birgir Isleifur Gunnarsson told Iceland state radio that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought $38 million of crowns during the morning. \par \par \uc2  That followed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  totalling some $50 million on Wednesday and Thursday, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  Gunnarsson declined to comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hike rates to support the crown. \par \par \uc2  "No decision has been made about raising interest rates," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to release the terms of its weekly repo \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1600 GMT, which would be one opportunity for it to announce a rate increase. \par \par \uc2  At 1410 the crown was trading at 79.73 bid per dollar, down from 79.12 at Thursday's close but off an earlier low of 80.62. \par \par \uc2  On its inverse trade-weighted index , followed closely by Icelandic banks and investors, it was about 114.90, down from Thursday's closing 114.19, after earlier going below 116 for the first time in nearly four years. \par \par \uc2  CROWN BUYERS RETURN \par \par \uc2  Landsbanki Islands hf (National Bank of Iceland) dealer Matthias Eynarsson said the market had been a one-way street in the last few days as the crown slid. \par \par \uc2  "Now market participants are returning who are willing to take a position in crowns, and that is creating the possibility for buyers and sellers to come together again in the market," he said. \par \par \uc2  The slide in the crown has been prompted by worries about inflation in the booming economy. The immediate crisis was prompted by a decline in the crown triggering stop-loss orders by corporates hedging foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowings. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said small investors were continuing to close short \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions on Friday, forcing the crown lower. \par \par \uc2  Bunadarbanki Islands hf (Agricultural Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Iceland\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) said in its daily newsletter that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the crown over the past two days had totalled some four billion crowns ($50.15 million). \par \par \uc2  "These are considerable amounts in the light of the effect on the market, although the crown might have weakened even more in the last couple of days had the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it said. \par \par \uc2  "An interest hike of up to 100 points can be expected in the near future." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last raised its repo rate in June, to 10.6 percent from 10.1 percent, taking the cumulative rise in the rate to 3.4 percentage points in about two years. \par \par \uc2  (Additional reporting by Jonathan Lynn in Stockholm) \par \par \uc2  ((Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1004, fax +46-8-211601, stockholm.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw7e09zkr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
